{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14255152,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":2,"pointsAwarded":2,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57964,"firstName":"William","lastName":"Parker","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO2MGD4gcTFRx970s7DzjQk","sequenceId":15},"course":{"id":76,"name":"Methods of Proof"},"topic":{"id":250,"name":"Conditional Statements"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T05:44:35.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T06:36:37.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T06:38:33.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T06:38:44.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62328727,"created":"2026-10-16T06:36:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11925,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 6:36 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":82092,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12704,"text":"<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <strong>If</strong> $7$ is an even number, <strong>then</strong> $6$ is an odd number. </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $6$ is an even number, <strong>then</strong> $7$ is an even number. </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $6$ is an even number, <strong>then</strong> $7$ is an odd number. </li></ol>","choice1":"I and III only","choice2":"I only","choice3":"II only","choice4":"I, II, and III","choice5":"III only","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>An implication $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true <em>unless</em> $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the &quot;promise&quot; is broken.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is true. The antecedent &quot;$7$ is an even number&quot; is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is <em>not</em> broken, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is false. The antecedent &quot;$6$ is an even number&quot; is true, and the consequent &quot;$7$ is an even number&quot; is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is true. The antecedent &quot;$6$ is an even number&quot; is true, and the consequent &quot;$7$ is an odd number&quot; is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is &quot;I and III only.&quot;</p>\n","topic":{"id":250,"name":"Conditional Statements"},"example":{"id":12704,"title":"Identifying True Conditional Statements"},"group":{"id":24477,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14255152,"answer":{"id":62328727,"cread":"2026-10-16T06:36:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11925},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62328746,"created":"2026-10-16T06:37:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12325,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 6:37 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":103482,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12704,"text":"<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <strong>If</strong> $-5 &gt; -2,$ <strong>then</strong> $-2 &lt;   -1.$ </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $-5 &lt;  -2 ,$ <strong>then</strong> $-2 &lt;   -1.$ </li><li>  <strong>If</strong> $-5 &gt; -2,$ <strong>then</strong> $-2 &gt; -1.$ </li></ol>","choice1":"I, II, and III\n","choice2":"II and III only\n","choice3":"I and III only\n","choice4":"II only","choice5":"III only","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>An implication $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true <em>unless</em> $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the &quot;promise&quot; is broken.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is true. The antecedent $-5 &gt; -2$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is <em>not</em> broken, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is true. The antecedent $-5 &lt;  -2$ is true, and the consequent $-2 &lt;   -1$ is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $-5 &gt; -2$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is <em>not</em> broken, and the statement is true.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is &quot;I, II, and III.&quot;</p>\n","topic":{"id":250,"name":"Conditional Statements"},"example":{"id":12704,"title":"Identifying True Conditional Statements"},"group":{"id":24109,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14255152,"answer":{"id":62328746,"cread":"2026-10-16T06:37:04.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12325},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62328799,"created":"2026-10-16T06:37:32.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[1,0,0,0]","timeElapsed":24866,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 6:37 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:25","question":{"id":182663,"format":"SS","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12705,"text":"<p> Find the missing values in the following truth table:</p>\n","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>First, we add columns for $\\neg P,$ $\\neg Q$ and $\\neg P \\lor \\neg Q{:}$</p></p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgc